      <div style="text-align: center; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;">
        <h2>What is MakerCreate?</h2>
        <p>MakerCreate is a YSWS (You Ship, We Ship) program @ HackClub. You spend time making hardware/CAD projects to create a new invention which didn't exist or something exist but has been improved on an approved editor, and we ship you parts or maybe a 3D printer of your own choice! (You can also spend earned logs on our <strong>MakerShop&trade;</strong>)</p>

        <h2>Rules and Guidelines of MakerCreate.</h2>
        <div class="ruleholder" style="justify-content: center;">
          <div class="rules" style="text-align: left;">
            <span>Eligibility Criteria:</span>
            <ul>
              <li>You MUST be 13-18 years old.</li>
              <li>You CANNOT be banned from Hackatime.</li>
              <li>You MUST be part of HackClub Slack.</li>
              <li>Your identity MUST be verified via <a href="https://auth.hackclub.com" class="links"  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HackClub Auth</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rules" style="text-align: left;">
            <span>Project Guidelines:</span>
            <ul>
              <li>You MUST spend at least 1 hour on your project.</li>
              <li>You MUST use one of our approved CAD software/Hardware platforms.</li>
              <li>You MUST use our lapse-based journaling system.</li>
              <li>Upload your project files to printables.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
